  "final_text": "All four steps are done. I didn't re-read the dashboard after the panel edit, so the new title is confirmed only by the update succeeding.\n\n- **Data view:** \"Kibana Sample Data Logs\" has the time field `timestamp`. The `response` field is a string, so the dashboard and the rule use `response.keyword`.\n- **Dashboard:** \"S4-88b91d3a Web logs\" has two panels. \"Requests over time\" is a line chart of request count by `timestamp`. \"Requests by response code\" is a bar chart of request count by `response.keyword`.\n- **Alert rule:** \"S4-88b91d3a 5xx errors\" is an `.es-query` rule that runs every minute. It fires when more than 10 requests have a response code from 500 to 599 within 5 minutes. The range is compared as text, which works because every code has three digits. It was created disabled, so I enabled it.\n- **Panel edit:** the response-code panel is now titled \"Responses by code\".\n- **Read-back:** the rule shows `enabled: true` and status `ok`.\n\nTIME_FIELD: timestamp\nRULE_ENABLED: yes",
